<refnamediv>
  <refname><varname>SilikoVersionPackageSuffix</varname></refname>
  <refpurpose>String holding packager’s version suffix</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Version.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">extern const char SilikoVersionPackageSuffix[];</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <varname>SilikoVersionPackageSuffix</varname> value holds a
suffix that packagers (such as for Linux distributions or other
repositories) can use to identify their particular package version.
<varname>SilikoVersionPackageSuffix</varname> is an empty string in
first-party releases and may be empty if the packager has no suffixing
scheme.</para>
</refsection>
